[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopResource.cs" id="1_shop"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopStockEntry.cs" id="2_entry"]

; Sedge Marrow, aboard the Wet Hull (Phase 38O) — the realm's first fence, and the discreet one.
;
; THE REFUSALS ARE THE DESIGN (38N1's rule, and it matters twice as much here). Sedge takes contraband,
; fine goods, stones and jewellery and NOTHING ELSE — no ore, no fish, no pelts, no iron. A fence who
; bought everything would be a general store with a reputation cost bolted on, and the walk down the
; water would buy the player nothing they could not get from Aldreth.
;
; ⚠️ FactionId IS EMPTY, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. The natural owner is faction.outlaws, which starts
; at -30 — tier Hostile, at or below its own HostileThreshold of 2 — so a shop factioned to it would be
; hidden by VendorComponent.ApplyPresence and refuse to trade from the first minute of a new game. The
; standing a fence MOVES and the standing she PRICES BY are two different questions, and 38O only
; answers the first. She therefore prices flat, at every tier, for everybody.
;
; The two-sided cost: +5 with the outlaws, -2 with the villagers, per sale rather than per unit. Six
; sales carry the outlaws from -30 to Neutral, at which point they stop being hostile on sight and the
; bandits on the road leave the player alone — a consequence that needed no new machinery at all,
; because EnemyAIComponent already reads IsHostile(faction.outlaws). The villagers' -2 is charged again
; at every honest counter in the realm through 38C's price ramp, forever. That is the trade.
;
; SellFraction 0.55 is the second-most generous in the game after Marta's 0.62, and it has to be: the
; player is paying a standing cost on top of walking here, and a fence who paid the ordinary 0.4 would
; be strictly worse than dumping the goods.
;
; PurseGold 260 with a 2-day clock is the brake instead. She is not a bottomless fence; a big haul
; needs two trips or two fences, which is why there are two.

